An organization uses SCPs to limit a departmental OU to EC2 and S3. The following SCP replaces FullAWSAccess at that OU; SCPs at every other level on the account path permit these actions.

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "ec2:*",
        "s3:*"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}

A newly created IAM user in a member account has no identity policies or group memberships. Its CreateBucket request is denied. Investigation finds no applicable explicit deny or other permission restriction.

What explains the result?
